*** ROUTER-vs-MAGIC LAYER OFFSET, CONFIRMED ON THIS DESIGN ***
The top cell's own routed polygons are on 68/20, 69/20, 70/20, 71/20 only --
there is NO 72/20 in the routing. So the router's glayer names are shifted one
step from the process layers:
    router met2 -> met1 (68/20)      router met4 -> met3 (70/20)
    router met3 -> met2 (69/20)      router met5 -> met4 (71/20)
routing_summary.txt's "met5, 413.11 um, 0.450 width" is physically met4.
Real met5 (72/20) appears ONLY inside the inductor cells (the spirals) --
which is why met5.2's 1.6 um spacing is a coil-to-coil placement concern and
never a routing concern on this design.

