PHASE 2 -- LVS
[L1] extract routed.gds + ignore class vco_spiral_ind on both circuits.
     MISMATCH: Magic fused coil ports A/B (equiv "B" "A"), collapsing
     VDD+voutp+voutn; 4 ports instead of 6; "Top level cell failed pin matching".
[L2] knob: property LEFview true on the coil before extract all.
     FAILED SILENTLY -- accepted with no error, coil still extracted, still
     shorted. Only visible effect: ext2spice now emitted the coil as
     `Xvco_spiral_ind_0 VDD VDD vco_spiral_ind`, i.e. the short made visible.
[L3] knob: deleted `equiv "B" "A"` from vco_spiral_ind.ext, added a real node
     "A", re-ran `ext2spice` alone (it reads .ext from disk without
     re-extracting -- a useful technique in itself).
     PARTIAL: voutn recovered (5 ports), voutp still fused, because the PARENT's
     hierarchical merges had already been written against the merged canonical
     node. Splitting a child cannot undo the parent's assignment.
[L4] knob: extraction-only GDS view. Deleted exactly one polygon -- the met5
     (72/20) spiral of cell vco_spiral_ind -- and re-added a 90,148-98,153 um
     met5 patch under port B. Kept both met4 landings, all 340 via4, both labels.
     MATCH, uniquely, with properties compared.
[L-neg] falsification: XN2 w=60 -> 42 in the schematic copy
     -> "Property errors were found". So w/l are genuinely compared.
