FINDINGS HANDED UP (not fixed here -- all are source fixes outside this gate)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Magic cannot extract an inductor -> the LVS gate for any circuit with a
   drawn spiral needs a scripted black-box view. Highest priority.
2. route_nets.py's corridor-clean check false-positives on stacked-plate
   macros: it predicted extraction shorts on XC0/XC1 that do not exist
   (both caps verified correctly wired, per plate and per layer).
3. The placer uses one global min_metal_spacing_um (0.14 um, glayout met2)
   and does not know met5's 1.6 um. Not triggered on this seed (coil gap
   1.6065 um) but latent on others.
4. generate_primitives.py::write_lvs_compare_netlist emits the tie-off dummy
   block before the LAST `.ends`, which in a multi-.subckt netlist is the last
   subckt, not the top one -- already hand-repaired upstream, per the header
   comment in lvs_compare.sp. Worth fixing at source.
